  "review": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "description": "W-CONFIGURATION-CHAT, W-EFFECTIVE-SETTINGS and W-CONFIGURATION-PROPOSAL receive credential-redacted native snapshots. Proposed safe edits remain readable and require their separate explicit confirmation. Credential edits and redacted placeholders are refused.",
    "implementation": "Reviewed nativeSnapshot/newNativeRedactor/value/text, native inspection in NativeConfig and dynamic, proposal construction, raw BeforeDigest confirmation/application checks, and startup sanitizeNativeProposal. Raw native responses remain transient and nativeOverrides remains unchanged; stored snapshots and diffs contain redacted values. Migration retains pending safe edits, stales credential edits and preserves historical freshness without replay. All work remains on existing background preparation/operation paths; no request-time I/O or cancellation deadline is introduced. Follow-up review fixes preserve native-generated layer selectors, distinguish nonsecret MCP argument/environment values from known credentials, collect credential URL components for copied-value redaction, and sanitize legacy proposal event data transactionally in pages of 32 while preserving sequence, kind, entity, timestamps, historical states and unrelated fields. Native named-entry containers distinguish identifier keys from actual credential setting keys; nativeKeyPath uses the existing TOML parser to preserve quoted identifiers and dotted project paths while validating the targeted setting context. Follow-up review corrections collect arbitrary custom-header values for masking in neutral copied-value fields and rejected edits. URL sanitization removes userinfo and credential-bearing query/fragment parameters while preserving exact noncredential URLs and bare anchors. Named-entry keys and short token-like provider references remain usable, nested credential fields remain protected, and multiline table documents are rejected as native key paths. The candidate serialization is named once in the edited validation predicate.",
    "tests": "Read TestNativeInspectionRedactsUnmanagedCredentials: both exported/native-agent inspection outputs exclude unmanaged credentials and retain exact profiles and layer versions without mutating native input. TestNativeProposalRetainsRedactedSnapshotAndRawFreshness requires a stored safe snapshot, unchanged public view after hidden password rotation, rejected stale confirmation and one exact fresh profile write. TestNativeCredentialEditsAreRejectedWithoutPersistence rejects nested env replacements, copied secret values, token patterns, credential URLs and placeholders without saved proposals/writes. TestNativeLegacyProposalMigrationPreservesStaleness checks safe migration, unchanged raw fingerprint, stale unsafe edits, no writes and idempotence. Existing race tests pass; live-host verification must be rerun after deployment. The selector/URL-copy regression exercises HOME, MODE and ordinary CLI values alongside a short URL password, token query and OAuth fragment, then proposes using the exact displayed file/version. Legacy migration now seeds real configuration events and 35 orphaned historical events, injects failure after one attempted update to prove rollback, verifies all pages and stable metadata/state, and compares repeated migration byte-for-byte. Inspection also asserts exact MaxInt64 numeric preservation. TestNativeCredentialWordsInNamesRemainEditable checks token/secret-scan/dotted profile names, a .secrets project path, plugin/server identifiers, whole-profile replacements and quoted native edits, while proving real API-key/password/environment fields inside those same named entries cannot bypass masking or edit rejection. Focused regressions first reproduced copied-header leakage, ordinary-URL loss, short sk-dev identifier masking and acceptance of copied header values. The corrected fixtures use arbitrary X-Auth and X-Workspace headers with copies under noncredential keys; shared inspection/proposal/legacy assertions exclude both values. The URL-password copy now uses ordinary_url_copy, so key masking cannot satisfy that assertion. TestNativeNonsecretURLsRemainEditable compares the exact public URL including transport/mode/profile query values and a bare secret-guide anchor through inspection, proposal and one confirmed native write, with no pre-confirmation write. Named-entry assertions also inspect the exact sk-dev provider reference and submit its safe edit; nested sk-dev API-key edits still reject. Rejection cases separately exercise query credentials, OAuth-fragment credentials and a table-form key path without persistence/writes. The table-form regression failed before its local validation guard."
  },
